<title>USA: Pulitzer February revenues up 17.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Pulitzer February revenues up 17.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pulitzer Publishing Co said Thursday its revenues rose 17.7 percent for the four weeks ended March 2 to $42.4 million from $36.0 million a year ago.</p>
<p>Year to date, the publishing company said revenues increased 17.1 percent to $90.4 million from $77.2 million.</p>
<p>It said Scripps League Newspapers Inc, renamed Pulitzer Community Newspapers Inc, added $4.9 million to February and $10.8 million to year-to-date revenues. Scripps was acquired on July 1, 1996.</p>
<p>		((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
